<%# English version of pages/privacy_policy.html.erb (French, the default and only binding version).
    Keep both files in step when the policy changes. %>
<% content_for :title, "Le Circographe - Privacy Policy" %>

<%= render layout: "shared/legal_page_shell" do %>
  <h2 class="mb-10 text-3xl font-bold text-center md:text-5xl">
    Privacy Policy
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-sm font-bold text-center sm:text-base">
    Last updated on 18 March 2025
  </p>
  <p class="mb-8 rounded-lg border border-brand-primary/20 bg-brand-primary/5 px-4 py-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
    This English version is an indicative translation. Only the French version of this policy is legally binding.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-8 text-sm sm:text-base">
    The privacy and security of your personal data matter greatly to Le Circographe. This Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, how we use it and the measures we take to protect it, in line with the GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation).
  </p>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">1. Data controller and contact</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      The controller of the data collected on Le Circographe is:
      <br />
      <strong>Association name:</strong> Le Circographe
      <br />
      <strong>Address:</strong> 97 bis Bd de Suisse, 31200 Toulouse
      <br />
      <strong>Email contact:</strong> contact@lecircographe.fr
      <br /><br />
      For any question about your personal data or to exercise your rights, you can contact us at the email address above.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">2. Data collected</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      <strong>2.1. Data you provide</strong>
      <br />
      When you become a member or take part in our activities, we collect:
      <br />
      • First and last name: to register and manage members.
      <br />
      • Email address: for communications and to manage your membership.
      <br />
      • Membership information: type and status of membership, membership dates.
      <br /><br />
      <strong>2.2. Data collected automatically</strong>
      <br />
      When you use our website or our systems, we automatically collect some data:
      <br />
      • Browsing data: IP address, browser type, pages visited, session length.
      <br />
      • Cookies: used to keep the website working and remember your preferences.
      <br /><br />
      <strong>2.3. Anonymised data</strong>
      <br />
      We collect anonymous data to analyse attendance at our activities and improve our services.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">3. Why we collect data</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      • <strong>Membership management:</strong> registering and following up memberships and contributions, organising activities and events.
      <br />
      • <strong>Communication:</strong> sending information about the association and its activities.
      <br />
      • <strong>Security:</strong> protection against fraudulent or unauthorised activity.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">4. How long we keep data</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      We keep your personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above:
      <br />
      • <strong>Membership data:</strong> kept while your membership is active. Deleted on request or once the legal retention period has ended.
      <br />
      • <strong>Browsing data:</strong> kept for 12 months for security and analysis purposes.
      <br />
      • <strong>Anonymised data:</strong> kept indefinitely for statistical analysis.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">5. Data sharing</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      Your personal data is never sold to third parties. It may however be shared in the following cases:
      <br />
      • <strong>Service providers:</strong> data hosting, technical maintenance.
      <br />
      • <strong>Legal obligations:</strong> disclosure to the competent authorities when required by law.
      <br /><br />
      All service providers are contractually bound to respect the confidentiality and security of your data.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">6. Cookies</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      <strong>6.1. Types of cookies used</strong>
      <br />
      • Functional cookies: essential for the website to work (sign-in, navigation).
      <br />
      • Analytics cookies: to assess general trends and improve the user experience.
      <br /><br />
      <strong>6.2. Consent</strong>
      <br />
      Functional cookies do not require consent. For any other type of cookie, a GDPR-compliant consent banner will be displayed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">7. Your rights</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      Under the GDPR, you have the following rights over your personal data:
      <br />
      • <strong>Right of access:</strong> you can ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you.
      <br />
      • <strong>Right to rectification:</strong> if your data is inaccurate or incomplete, you can ask for it to be corrected.
      <br />
      • <strong>Right to erasure:</strong> you have the right to ask for your personal data to be deleted.
      <br />
      • <strong>Right to data portability:</strong> your data can be provided to you in a readable, transferable format.
      <br />
      • <strong>Right to object:</strong> you can object to the processing of your data in some cases.
      <br /><br />
      To exercise your rights, contact us at contact@lecircographe.fr. Proof of identity may be requested.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">8. Data security</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      We apply strict technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data:
      <br />
      • Encryption of sensitive data.
      <br />
      • HTTPS/SSL to secure exchanges.
      <br />
      • Regular backups to prevent data loss.
      <br />
      • Access restricted to authorised administrators.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">9. Children's protection</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      Our platform is not specifically intended for children. If we find out that a minor is using our services, we will take the necessary steps to protect their data.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">10. Disputes and contact</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      If there is a dispute about your personal data, we encourage you to contact us at contact@lecircographe.fr. We will do our best to address your concerns. If you believe your rights have not been respected, you can also file a complaint with the CNIL (the French data protection authority).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-y-3">
    <p class="font-bold uppercase sm:text-base">11. Changes to this policy</p>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
      This Privacy Policy may change to reflect:
      <br />
      • Legal or regulatory changes.
      <br />
      • Changes to our activities or services.
      <br /><br />
      We will inform users of any changes by email or through a notice on the website.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="my-8 min-h-[1px] min-w-full bg-gray-300"></div>
  <p class="mb-6 text-sm sm:text-base">
    By using our services, you accept this Privacy Policy in full. If you have any questions, feel free to contact us.
  </p>
<% end %>
